<!-- The kill glyph (owner, 2026-09-02). It was a circled cross, which sat next to the sheet's
     dismiss — also a cross — and one of the two is irreversible in consequence. A skull cannot
     be confused with "close", and it says what the tool does without a word.

     Stroked outline in the set's own weight (1.4), with the sockets and nose FILLED: a purely
     stroked skull is illegible at 18 dp, and dark sockets are what makes the shape read. Used
     both in the specimen header and as the armed kill tool in the dial. -->
